WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.103
STEPHANIE WONG: If you
are new to Google Cloud,

00:00:02.103 --> 00:00:03.520
it can sometimes
feel like there's

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.440
a lot of information
to absorb when

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.510
trying to decide
what to use because

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:10.010
of the huge list of
products available.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.760
So this is why we created
a new and simplified page

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.130
to help you get started
quickly on Google Cloud

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.530
in a handy five-part menu.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.110
Just head to cloud.google.com,
then Getting Started.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.020
Let me give you a quick tour.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.880
For starters, we have three
main essential buckets.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.560
The first is learning how
to sign up for a free trial.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.530
The second is exploring how
to try out different products

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.660
via our quick start tutorials.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.330
And the third is, once you
are ready to get started

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.180
with Google Cloud, you can
review common developer use

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.350
cases or an
enterprise checklist.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.810
When you scroll down
a bit more, for those

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.610
who are looking for
a macro-level view

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.500
of our entire
suite of offerings,

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.190
our amazing team has put
together a helpful color-coded

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.110
cheat sheet listing
all our products

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.930
and their functions
in four words or less

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.460
and their respective features
that you can hover over.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.170
We also have
documented guides that

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:09.010
range from giving you a bird's
eye overview of Google Cloud

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:13.030
or compare Cloud services
with Azure and AWS,

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:16.450
as well as review architecture
references, diagrams,

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.520
design patterns,
and best practices

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.150
for migrating your
workloads to Google Cloud.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.310
Oh, and here is
my favorite place.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:28.330
Stay in the know with developer
news and community resources

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:30.610
by checking out the
Developer Center

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.860
to join our dev community.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.190
And join the Google
Cloud Innovators Program,

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.080
where you can
receive invitations

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.230
to hear from Google Cloud
executives and developer

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.620
advocates, like myself;
see roadmap presentations;

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.980
and a chance for an invitation
to join our new series

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.470
of innovator community events.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:54.010
It's kind of like that
VIP club at Disneyland.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.690
The Dev Center
features highlights

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:57.850
like our new
architecture diagramming

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.970
tool, where you can build
architecture diagrams,

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.560
see reference architectures, and
even do one-click deployments

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.900
directly to Google Cloud.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.330
And now that we got a
high-level overview,

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.800
let me walk you through a
couple of different examples.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.640
Let's take a look at some of
the quick start tutorials.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.940
You can browse the catalog
or search for a specific item

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.000
to learn more, whether it's
on getting started topics,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.820
like security,
enabling APIs, using

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:30.880
the command-line interface
SDK called gcloud,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.310
creating workflows,
identity and logins,

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.800
performing
investigations, et cetera.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.140
There are also more
advanced specific topics,

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:43.390
like databases, storage options,
container VMs, private IPs,

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.260
hosting of web apps or services,
machine learning, and more.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:50.260
When you head to common
developer use cases,

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.410
we have a mix of useful
videos and articles organized

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.530
under a range of topics
in a friendly interface.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.290
When you are ready to learn
how to build on Google Cloud,

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:02.950
we also have launched an
improved documentation home

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.270
page so that you can more easily
find guides, code samples,

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:10.900
tutorials, and API references,
in addition to our architecture

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.320
assets.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.020
And there you have it, a
quick walkthrough of our new

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.950
getting started resources.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.800
We hope that you check them out.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.820
For now, this is Stephanie Wong.

